    ["它是湖里一只安静的巨龟。\n它看过很多年风吹过湖面，也看过很多人来来去去。 \n岸边来了会流血的人，会祈祷的人，会变成石像的人，湖水变得越来越暖，暖得发胀，暖得发痛，每一寸血肉都在疯长， 连呼吸都像要裂开。\n它开始在水面上旋转、跳跃、咆哮， 挡住每一个想靠近湖心的人。 它分不清自己是在驱赶别人， 还是在向谁求救。"] = "It is a quiet giant turtle in the lake. \n It has watched the wind blow across the lake for many years, and it has watched many people come and go. \n People who bleed, people who pray, and people who turn into stone statues have come to the shore. The lake water has become warmer and warmer, warm to the point of swelling, warm to the point of pain. Every inch of flesh is growing wildly, and even breathing feels like it is about to tear apart. \n It begins to spin, jump, and roar on the surface of the water, blocking everyone who tries to approach the center of the lake. It cannot tell if it is driving others away or calling for help from someone.",
